# Step 28, its third pull request's first part: custom commands, the
# second review's fixes (a command sent through a lane that its session's
# close did not reach, a command's question still open when the running
# turn stops, an interrupt's own step that reached commands sent after it,
# a sent command's run left on the session by a step refused before it
# began, and a command of an extension not loaded refused with why),
# broken one at a time, with the tests that must fail.

[break] a-sent-commands-token-is-below-one-nothing-holds
rule: A command sent through a lane has a token of its own below the session's, which its run holds, so that the session's close and the core's shutdown reach it.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/commands.rs
in: sent
find:
    crate::core::lock(&live.running_commands).push(Running {
        id,
        cancel,
        kill,
        lane: true,
    });
replace:
    crate::core::lock(&live.running_commands).push(Running {
        id,
        cancel: cancel.child(),
        kill,
        lane: true,
    });
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it commands_lane::a_queued_command_is_interrupted_and_a_running_turns_stop_refuses_a_commands_host_calls
    cineris-core::it commands::a_command_runs_nothing_where_its_prompt_would_be_refused_and_its_stop_is_the_sessions

[break] a-commands-host-call-allowed-after-its-turn-stopped-runs
rule: A command's host call whose question was open when the turn running as it runs was stopped is refused with that stop once it is allowed.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/host.rs
in: CallHost::decide
find: match self.parts.policy.stopped_for_hooks(self.cx.turn) {
replace: match None::<String> {
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it commands_lane::a_queued_command_is_interrupted_and_a_running_turns_stop_refuses_a_commands_host_calls

[break] an-interrupts-step-stops-commands-sent-after-it
rule: An interrupt sent through a lane reaches only the commands sent before it: its own step, run in the lane's order, leaves a command sent behind it to run.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/commands.rs
in: interrupt
find: .filter(|run| !run.lane || run.id < before)
replace: .filter(|_| true)
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it commands_lane::a_queued_command_is_interrupted_and_a_running_turns_stop_refuses_a_commands_host_calls

[break] a-refused-commands-step-leaves-its-run-on-the-session
rule: A command's step takes the run put on the session as it was sent before anything can refuse it, so that a step refused before it begins leaves nothing that a later command of the same client and call takes.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/core.rs
in: Core::handle_op
find: let live = self.live(&params.session_id)?;
replace: let live = self.open_for(client, &params.session_id)?;
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it commands_lane::a_queued_command_is_interrupted_and_a_running_turns_stop_refuses_a_commands_host_calls

[break] an-unloaded-extensions-command-is-refused-without-why
rule: A command of an extension the session found and does not load is refused with why, as the session was told it: changed since it was approved, or not approved.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/commands.rs
in: expand
find: live.command_hooks.scripts.why_not_loaded(extension)
replace: None::<String>
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it commands::a_command_runs_nothing_where_its_prompt_would_be_refused_and_its_stop_is_the_sessions
